<title>UK: Kingfisher rises after &quot;buy&quot; recommendation.</title>
<headline>Kingfisher rises after &quot;buy&quot; recommendation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK retailer Kingfisher Plc rose on Friday after SBC Warburg repeated its &quot;buy&quot; recommendation on the stock, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares rose 6p to 618-1/2p by 0958 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;Basically they are saying that things are going extremely well at Kingfisher, particularly at B&amp;Q,&quot; said a market source.</p>
<p>Dealers said buyers emerged after the shares fell 6p yesterday.</p>
<p>Shares in Boots Plc were up 4-1/2p to 607-1/2p in a firmer retail sector, traders said. --Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
